{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25599718",
      "title": "Class-based Components & Context",
      "sourceHash": "d43079bc5833c9975e2b5e06381dfce21aa8eba6330f461897b216148db3c349",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.16,
          "en": "Now what about context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.16,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "and class space components?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 9.24,
          "en": "Well the first important takeaway is that you can still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.24,
          "end": 14.24,
          "en": "define it and provide it as you learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.25,
          "end": 18.12,
          "en": "You define it by calling create context, maybe with some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.12,
          "end": 22.713,
          "en": "initial value and you then provide it by using the provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.713,
          "end": 27.01,
          "en": "component which is part of that creative context object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.01,
          "end": 30.38,
          "en": "And then you can pass a value to that and here it's actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.38,
          "end": 34.89,
          "en": "a static value which never changes, but it also may change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 39.07,
          "en": "with state updates and that all doesn't change only the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.07,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "you update state of course changes if you use a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 45.82,
          "en": "based component, as explained over the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.82,
          "end": 48.84,
          "en": "As a side note, if you want to follow along, attached you'll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 53.01,
          "en": "find the updated app component and this users context JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 57.92,
          "en": "file which you can add into a newly created store folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.92,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "But back to that, here we provide as we learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 65.15,
          "en": "The only part which changes when you're working with context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 65.15,
          "end": 70.15,
          "en": "is related to how you use it in your class based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 70.77,
          "end": 73.42099999999999,
          "en": "Now I haven't edit any code for using context up until",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.42099999999999,
          "end": 78.35,
          "en": "now so therefore let's go to the user finder and think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 78.35,
          "end": 80.445,
          "en": "about how we could add it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 80.445,
          "end": 83.96600000000001,
          "en": "There let's say I no longer wanna work with the dummy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 83.96600000000001,
          "end": 88.96600000000001,
          "en": "users defined in this file, I no longer wanna get my data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.6,
          "end": 93.88,
          "en": "from there, but instead I want to get my data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93.88,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "from context, because it's managed application wide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 99.78999999999999,
          "end": 103.64,
          "en": "If this would be a functional component, we would of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 103.64,
          "end": 108.64,
          "en": "used the use context hook for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 108.68,
          "end": 111.65,
          "en": "That's what we would do, but this is not an option here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 111.65,
          "end": 113.997,
          "en": "in the class based component because we can't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 113.997,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "use hooks there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 119.511,
          "en": "Instead here we got two ways of using context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 119.511,
          "end": 124.511,
          "en": "One approach was shown to you early in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 125.091,
          "end": 130.091,
          "en": "The context consumer component can be used in both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 130.72,
          "end": 133.405,
          "en": "functional and class based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 133.405,
          "end": 138.108,
          "en": "So in your render method you could import the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 138.108,
          "end": 142.1,
          "en": "context, so add it here and of course import it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 142.1,
          "end": 144.75900000000001,
          "en": "from the users context file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 144.75900000000001,
          "end": 149.75900000000001,
          "en": "And then simply add that consumer or access this consumer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 150.16,
          "end": 153.59,
          "en": "component and then use it as showed to you early",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 153.59,
          "end": 155.09,
          "en": "in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 155.09,
          "end": 159.41,
          "en": "Since this is used in JSX only it works in both functional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 159.41,
          "end": 161.053,
          "en": "and class based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 161.98,
          "end": 165.89,
          "en": "But the user hook is used so that we don't have to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 165.89,
          "end": 167.43,
          "en": "this consumer component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 167.43,
          "end": 169.84,
          "en": "So what's the equivalent to this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 169.84,
          "end": 174.35399999999998,
          "en": "There is no perfect equivalent, I will say that right away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 174.35399999999998,
          "end": 179.35399999999998,
          "en": "With use context, you can listen to multiple context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 179.719,
          "end": 183.91,
          "en": "in one of the same component by calling use context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 183.91,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "multiple times and pointing at different contexts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 191.87,
          "en": "This will not be possible with class based components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 191.87,
          "end": 196,
          "en": "because there you can only connect a class based component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 196,
          "end": 198.43,
          "en": "to one context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 198.43,
          "end": 202.15,
          "en": "And you do that by adding a static property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 202.15,
          "end": 207.11,
          "en": "by adding the static keyword here and then adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 207.11,
          "end": 211.89,
          "en": "the property named context type written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 211.89,
          "end": 216.37,
          "en": "And then you assign a value of users context here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 216.37,
          "end": 220.3,
          "en": "With that you're telling React hey this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 220.3,
          "end": 223.874,
          "en": "should have access to the user's context context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 223.874,
          "end": 227.97,
          "en": "but you can only set the static context type property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 227.97,
          "end": 231.62,
          "en": "once so if there are two contexts which should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 231.62,
          "end": 235.1,
          "en": "connected to one at the same component, this would simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 235.1,
          "end": 237.68,
          "en": "not be an option, you would have to find some other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 237.68,
          "end": 240.457,
          "en": "work around like wrapping it in a number component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 240.457,
          "end": 242.413,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 242.413,
          "end": 247.079,
          "en": "With that said however, you can then simply access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 247.079,
          "end": 252.079,
          "en": "this context users in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 254.12,
          "end": 257.883,
          "en": "in all the places where you need access to the users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 261.24,
          "end": 265.85,
          "en": "And with that, it will again work as before as you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 265.85,
          "end": 268.75,
          "en": "tell but now with context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 268.75,
          "end": 272.498,
          "en": "So it is all quite straightforward to use but a bit less",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 272.498,
          "end": 277.07,
          "en": "flexible than in the functional component world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 277.07,
          "end": 280.55,
          "en": "Of course you will not always need more than one context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 280.55,
          "end": 285.05,
          "en": "per component, often one context is enough but if you do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 285.05,
          "end": 288.46,
          "en": "need more contexts connected to one component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 288.46,
          "end": 291.493,
          "en": "then this restriction can of course hurt.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}